# --- Entry 52: the A-chain -------------------------------------------------

:h_e52build a prov:Activity ; p-plan:correspondsToStep "src/harness/e52_build.py" ; prov:used :i_d36_fr_rider ;
    rdfs:comment "The only expensive step (~12 min): walks D3–D6 once and caches per-form energy components at every τ grid point, so every downstream fit in Entries 52–72 is exact arithmetic (the forms are linear in ε). Arms: E52_AERO=seg|reg, E52_FALLBACK=prior|rider — non-default arms suffix the cache (.seg/.prior), the unsuffixed cache is reg+rider." .
:o_e52_aggregates a :Output ; dcterms:identifier "e52_aggregates.csv" ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy :h_e52build ; :input :i_d36_fr_rider ;
    :transformer :F1, :F2, :F3, :F4, :F_base, :F_invert ; :cardinality 2039 ;
    :selection "every scored D3–D6 ride; the cache every second-order output of Entries 52–72 joins on" ;
    rdfs:comment "Suffixed arms e52_aggregates.seg.csv / .prior.csv (2,039 each) carry the Entry 55/57 comparisons. verify() checks the cache against FRESH approximate() calls at ε values neither endpoint used (2.2e-16) after the original check was found to only ever return zero." .

:h_e52split a prov:Activity ; p-plan:correspondsToStep "src/harness/e52_split.py" ; prov:used :o_e52_aggregates ;
    rdfs:comment "A.1–A.8: 15% of each corpus held out once (seed 48), repeated stratified 5-fold × 4 with EVERY free parameter (ε, τ, c, x_flat) refitted in-fold, CV binding (mean |log(Ê/E)|) with AIC reported, test scored once — the scoring routine refuses to run until the validation winner is serialised." .
:o_e52_split a :Output ; dcterms:identifier "e52_split.csv" ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy :h_e52split ; :input :i_d36_fr_rider ; :transformer :F1, :F2, :F3, :F4 ;
    :cardinality 4 ;
    :selection "grain is the FORM (train CV + one test scoring each); 1,734 train / 305 test rides underneath" ;
    rdfs:comment "The canonical rows are the reg-aero + rider-fallback chain (Entries 55/57 re-based the defaults): F3 wins at CV 0.05406, ε = 0.2939, τ = 6 m, test 3.24 [2.75, 3.50]. The seg sensitivity arm lives in e52_split.seg.csv (4 rows). Downstream harnesses READ fitted constants from this CSV — never a literal (the e54/e61 held-parameter lesson)." .
:o_e52_summary a :Output ; dcterms:identifier "e52_summary.csv" ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy :h_e52split ; :cardinality 18 ;
    :selection "the gate-facing summary (what bootstrap_ci.py section 3q reads); seg arm suffixed .seg (10 rows)" .

:entry52 a :Statistic ; rdfs:label "Entry 52 — one protocol, one split: P_{a,g} retired, F3 selected held-out" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom :o_e52_split, :o_e52_summary ; :gatedBy :gate ;
    rdfs:comment "F3 the only form inside the 1-SE band; CV and AIC agree. D1/D2 revealed as re-processings of D5 (87% of D2 matches on measured kJ) — they survive as history, not evidence. F_base scored WORST with a −3.85 São Paulo bias, diagnosed as the inversion protocol (quasi-steady constants spent on transients), confirmed by intervention in Entry 55. Claim wording licensed by the split: given a ride's own constants, the form and a universal ε reproduce its energy on rides that chose neither. Disclosure printed with the headline: 82% of test rides have a same-rider train ride within 5% distance / 10% ascent — a repeat-route error. Gate section 3q." .

:entry53 a :Statistic ; rdfs:label "Entry 53 — joint linear inversion of the constants: REFUTED" ;
    rdfs:comment "No journal heading and no canonical CSV of its own — the negative result lives in the commit (src/harness/e53_linear_invert.py) and is cited by Entries 55/67. Its direction (pool at rider level where a ride cannot support a fit) became Entry 57." .

# --- Entries 54–59: the physics made honest --------------------------------

:h_e54 a prov:Activity ; p-plan:correspondsToStep "src/harness/e54_transfer.py" ; prov:used :o_e52_aggregates .
