    prov:wasGeneratedBy :h_e54 ; :input :i_d36_fr_rider ; :transformer :F3 ;
    :cardinality 31 ;
    :selection "grain is the (donor × recipient) pair — 7 riders, donors fitted on train halves only, scored on OTHER riders' test halves" ;
    rdfs:comment "The corrected output. The first run fitted donors at TAU_PUB_I = 2 m while the selected form uses 6 m — a held parameter that manufactured a negative transfer penalty and a spurious case for rider-weighted pooling (caught in Entry 59). Its pooled comparator was also once a hardcoded 0.2879 that went stale when the aero estimator changed; both now read from the producing CSVs." .

:entry54 a :Statistic ; rdfs:label "Entry 54 — leave-one-rider-out ε transfer: +0.047 pp" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom :o_e54 ; :gatedBy :gate ;
    rdfs:comment "The paper's one real hypothesis: a published ε serves a rider who contributed nothing to it. Corrected penalty +0.047 pp [0.033, 0.084] — under Entry 48's 1.0 pp margin, so the transfer claim stands (scoped by Entry 60 to WITHIN a region; across regions costs 0.85 pp). Gate section 3r." .

:entry55 a :Statistic ; rdfs:label "Entry 55 — regime-consistent aero adopted as the default" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom :o_e52_split, :o_e52_aggregates ; :gatedBy :gate ;
    rdfs:comment "Swapping ONLY the CdA estimator (seg → reg, i.e. drag inferred at the MEASURED flat speed): F3 test 3.98 → 3.39, bias −1.06 → +0.06, and F_base's São Paulo bias −3.85 → −0.03 — Entry 52's diagnosis confirmed by intervention; the 190/305 'win' over the simulation becomes 149/305, p = 0.73: parity. Carried honestly: τ refits 2 → 6 m (the deadband was part-compensating aero error) and F4 wins the test half while F3 wins binding CV. The seg arm is retained as the sensitivity pair (e52_split.seg.csv)." .

:h_e56 a prov:Activity ; p-plan:correspondsToStep "src/harness/e56_struct.py" ; prov:used :o_e52_aggregates .
