:entry62 a :Statistic ; rdfs:label "Entry 62 — what the corpora ARE: the descriptive profile" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom :o_e62 ;
    rdfs:comment "Fits nothing, gates nothing — the missing denominator after sixty inferential entries. Headline: heart rate does NOT separate the corpora (medians 128–148 bpm) while mechanical output spans 2.9× — D5 produces 0.68 W/beat vs 1.28–1.40 for the road riders; the first MEASURED support for Entry 61's conclusion. Also: D5 is an urban commuting corpus (moving fraction 0.85, 67% of rides < 0.9); moving fraction elsewhere is auto-pause, a device statistic, unusable as behaviour; D6a's bpm rests on 22/194 rides (no strap) and D6d is 14 rides — included for completeness, not inference." .

# --- Entries 63–70: the F5 program -----------------------------------------

