    prov:wasGeneratedBy :h_e63 ; :transformer :F3, :F5f, :F5m ; :cardinality 7 ;
    :selection "grain is the RECIPIENT rider (Entry 54's strictness: donors' train halves → recipient's test half); the τ_n = {0, 3, 4.5} and rainflow/smooth LORO arms are suffixed siblings" .
:o_e63_taupred_t2 a :Output ; dcterms:identifier "e63_taupred.E63_TAUN2p0.csv" ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy :h_e63 ; :cardinality 7 ;
    :selection "grain is the rider GROUP: fitted τ* vs the τ_n + h_KE/2(1−ε) prediction" .

:entry63 a :Statistic ; rdfs:label "Entry 63 — F5 benchmarked: the deadband is mostly the KE buffer" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom :o_e63_tolls, :o_e63_split ;
    rdfs:comment "F5 beats its pinned-τ control at both floors and is the first form ever to enter F3's 1-SE band (at τ_n = 2); the fitted deadband's job is ~four-fifths reproducible as jitter filter + parameter-free toll. v_b rails at never-brake — the cap doesn't bind at these corpora's grades. Winner under the registered rule stays F3 in THIS entry; the τ_n = 2 test scoring follows Entry 55's sensitivity-arm precedent." .

:entry64 a :Statistic ; rdfs:label "Entry 64 — F5f wins selection; F5m transfers better; the τ* ordering prediction fails" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom :o_e63_split_t2, :o_e63_loro_t2, :o_e63_taupred_t2 ;
    rdfs:comment "F5f (1 parameter) inside F3's 1-SE band → selection flips to the computed toll; AIC still prefers F3, stated per Entry 49's precedent. F5m closer on 169/302 LORO rides (p = 0.044), biggest gain on D5, the rider most unlike the donors. τ* ordering vs h_KE: ρ = +0.055 — magnitude right, ordering bias-contaminated (Entry 39's lesson under a sharper lens). Multiplicity stated: the seed-48 test half has now been scored by seven registered estimators. The filterless amendment (τ_n = 0) prices the decomposition: toll alone 53% of the F2→F3 gap, filter alone 76%, both 82% — ~46 pp shared; the deadband is NOT redundant (without it F5f leaves the band and the LORO significance dissolves)." .

:entry65 a :Statistic ; rdfs:label "Entry 65 — rainflow and smoothing both fail; the unique share named (then refuted in 66)" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom :o_e63_tolls ;
    rdfs:comment "Outputs: the e63_{tolls,split,loro}.E63_TAUN0p0_E63_RAINFLOW1 / _E63_SMOOTH15 families (2,039 / 6 / 7 rows). Rainflow OVER-tolls (39% of the gap; the only arm where v_b left the rail, fitting 32 km/h — the optimiser shrinking buffers to undo it: hierarchy without per-context entry speed is worse than none). σ = 15 smoothing is inert alone (0%) and buys the toll 2 pp. The surviving attribution — amplitude-bounded long-wavelength error, i.e. barometric drift — was Entry 66's target. Filterless program closed; F5f(τ_n = 2) stays the best variant." .

:h_e66 a prov:Activity ; p-plan:correspondsToStep "src/harness/e66_driftprobe.py" ;
    rdfs:comment "Re-parses raw records for lat/lon (the pts cache keeps no geo). Its record loader is a deliberate LOCAL COPY: param_fit.py is a module-level script whose import runs Entry 15 and rewrites param_fit.csv — which it did once in this entry's smoke before the copy." .
