    :selection "one row per ride; 1,663 with ≥ 10 closure pairs carry statistics (median 393 pairs/ride)" ;
    rdfs:comment "Scalar statistics ONLY — the repo is public and no ride geometry leaves the walk. This CSV is also the PIN SOURCE for F5p and paper 2's F5 floors: consumers read the medians from it, never hardcode them." .

:entry66 a :Statistic ; rdfs:label "Entry 66 — drift measured (2.8 m, 3.4 m/h), Entry 65's attribution refuted at ride grain" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom :o_e66 ;
    rdfs:comment "The drift is real and baro-sized, but the deadband's τ6-over-τ2 benefit is BLIND to it (ρ = −0.009, n = 1,413) and rider-level τ* anti-correlates with drift. Re-reading adopted: the fitted deadband's unique share is the model's cheapest flexible misfit absorber, not measurement-error removal. S2 (drift correction) deferred with a registered predicted-null." .

:h_e67 a prov:Activity ; p-plan:correspondsToStep "src/harness/e67_residual.py" ;
    rdfs:comment "Pins the e63 module to the τ_n = 2 arm BEFORE import; pure cache arithmetic; train half only — the test half untouched." .
:o_e67_signature a :Output ; dcterms:identifier "e67_signature.csv" ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy :h_e67 ; :cardinality 1732 ;
    :selection "train-half rides: per-ride removal effect δ at common ε vs signed misfit r — the coupling that is the ONLY channel through which τ = 6 can beat τ = 2 once ε is refit per arm" .
:o_e67_stability a :Output ; dcterms:identifier "e67_stability.csv" ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy :h_e67 ; :cardinality 6 ;
    :selection "grain is the rider-HALF pair: (ε, τ*) refit early/late, plus the aging test (late half under early constants, F3 vs F5f)" .

:entry67 a :Statistic ; rdfs:label "Entry 67 — no transferable physics in the deadband's unique share" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom :o_e67_signature, :o_e67_stability ;
    rdfs:comment "Coupling weak everywhere (pooled ρ +0.082, within +0.081, between −0.029 — neither the physics nor the absorber fingerprint); τ* moved in 5/6 riders early→late; aging medians F3 0.00298 vs F5f 0.00064 — the deadbanded form's early constants serve the same rider's later rides ~4.7× worse. What transfers is exactly F5f's content: ε + the computed toll are stationary within riders. D4 flagged as the counterexample (a material mid-history change; device or route-mix shift suspected)." .

:entry68 a :Statistic ; rdfs:label "Entry 68 — the τ_n sweep: the floor is load-bearing; only a measurement can pin it" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom :o_e63_tolls, :o_e66 ;
    rdfs:comment "Eight floors (the e63_tolls.E63_TAUN* family); summary is console-borne, reproducible per arm via E63_TAUN=<x> E63_F5FCV=1. F5f's CV declines MONOTONICALLY to the F3 anchor (F5f(6) ≡ F3(6), ε recovering 0.2939 to the third decimal — the predicted degeneracy landing exactly) while the toll margin decays 0.0047 → 0. No data-internal floor exists; the registered pin is Entry 66's measured drift amplitude (median 2.8 m), making τ_n telemetry per corpus." .

:h_e69 a prov:Activity ; p-plan:correspondsToStep "src/harness/e69_frontier.py" ;
    rdfs:comment "Pins read from e66_drift.csv, F3's CV read from the chain CSV — never hardcoded; errors out listing any missing toll walk rather than tolling zero. Cross-checked digit-for-digit against the standalone e63_loro/e67_stability τ_n = {3, 4.5} runs." .
:o_e69_pins a :Output ; dcterms:identifier "e69_pins.csv" ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy :h_e69 ; prov:wasDerivedFrom :o_e66 ; :cardinality 7 ;
    :selection "grain is the rider GROUP: median measured drift snapped to the cached τ grid — F5p's floors" .
:o_e69_frontier a :Output ; dcterms:identifier "e69_frontier.csv" ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy :h_e69 ; :transformer :F3, :F5f, :F5p ; :cardinality 5 ;
    :selection "grain is the FORM (train CV; no test-half scoring happened in this entry)" .
:o_e69_loro a :Output ; dcterms:identifier "e69_loro.csv" ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy :h_e69 ; :transformer :F3, :F5p ; :cardinality 7 ;
    :selection "grain is the RECIPIENT rider" .
:o_e69_aging a :Output ; dcterms:identifier "e69_aging.csv" ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy :h_e69 ; :cardinality 6 ;
    :selection "grain is the RIDER: late half scored under early-half constants, per form" .

:entry69 a :Statistic ; rdfs:label "Entry 69 — the frontier collapses; F5p; the flat-basin law named" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom :o_e69_pins, :o_e69_frontier, :o_e69_loro, :o_e69_aging ;
    rdfs:comment "Keepability is FLAT in the floor (aging ~0.0006 at every rung vs F3's 0.0030): what ages badly in F3 is the τ REFIT, not the removal size. F5p — zero chosen constants, ε the only fitted parameter — matches F3's CV (0.05413 vs 0.05406), ages ~4× better, posts the program's best rider transfer (−0.27 pp [−0.50, −0.13], 184/301, p = 0.0001). The flat-basin law: where the loss is locally flat, fitting harvests noise, and fitted noise is precisely what does not generalise (E39/E50/E51/E67–69 are the same principle). Closing reframe adopted: F5 is the DERIVATION'S WITNESS — F3 stays the published form. Untested axis stated: LORO holds out riders, not landscapes." .

:h_e70 a prov:Activity ; p-plan:correspondsToStep "src/harness/e70_taucurves.py" ; prov:used :o_e52_aggregates .
:o_e70 a :Output ; dcterms:identifier "e70_taucurves.csv" ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy :h_e70 ; :transformer :F3 ; :cardinality 153 ;
    :selection "grain is the (pool × τ) cell: 9 pools × 17 grid points, train half, ε refit per point — deliberately IN-SAMPLE per group: the object is basin SHAPE, not a generalisation estimate" .

:entry70 a :Statistic ; rdfs:label "Entry 70 — pinned-τ curves per rider: basins are rider-shaped" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom :o_e70 ;
    rdfs:comment "The pooled-EU curve's steepness is ONE rider: D6-user_3 runs monotonically to the 12 m grid RAIL (the absorber signature in its purest form) while two other Europeans own the flattest basins in the family — a pooled curve inherits its steepest member (E59's lesson again). In-pool optima ANTI-track measured drift row by row. Open diagnosis flagged: what does user_3's ledger systematically overpredict?" .

# --- Entries 71–72: papers 2 and 3 -----------------------------------------

:h_e71 a prov:Activity ; p-plan:correspondsToStep "src/harness/e41_dem_route.py (E41_POP=p1 E41_D6=1) + src/harness/e71_dem_pop.py" ;
    prov:used :i_e71_dem ;
    rdfs:comment "MODE runs suffix the CSV AND the sampling cache and skip the published gates — the canonical e41 walk (:o_e41, gate 3i) is untouched. The valley toll is e63's ride_tolls called with the module floor set per call: one algebra copy." .
:o_e41_mode a :Output ; dcterms:identifier "e41_dem_route.E41_POPp1_E41_D61.csv" ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy :h_e71 ; :input :i_e71_dem ; :transformer :F3, :F4, :F5, :F_v2edge ;
    :cardinality 1957 ;
    :selection "1,957 rides walked; the PRIMARY population is 1,834 (D3+D4+D5 1,164 with D5's 84 travel rides kept via the per-ride igc_ok flag, D6 670) — survey arms absent on travel rides, not rides dropped" .
:o_e71 a :Output ; dcterms:identifier "e71_dem_pop.csv" ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy :h_e71 ; :cardinality 97 ;
    :selection "grain is the (table × pool × arm) summary cell over the MODE walk: re-based Table 1, the c(τ) grids, the paired terrain split, F5 per floor" .

:entry71 a :Statistic ; rdfs:label "Entry 71 — paper 2 re-based: travel rides, D6 vs FABDEM, c(τ), F5 on planner inputs" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom :o_e41_mode, :o_e71, :o_e66 ; :gatedBy :gate ;
    rdfs:comment "D6 vs FABDEM prices like São Paulo (the prescription transfers; D6 baro 3.4 · +0.3 is the program's cleanest column). The within-rider terrain split: same rider, fab5, covered 5.7 vs travel 7.7 (paired +5.1 → +7.2) while their barometer holds 4.7 — the terrain caveat at fixed person and instrument. c(τ) per chain: European chains 2.4× cleaner (D6 baro 1.26 vs SP 3.01 m/km) with ρ(c, ruggedness) positive within every corpus — c is sensor noise convolved with terrain reversal structure; never inherit a c. F5 beats F3 on EVERY DEM chain, best floor at the chain's measured noise scale (fab5 SP 5.06 → 3.67). Honesty note: this F3 carries the letter's frozen τ = 2 bundle. Gate section 3j (canonical 3i untouched)." .

:h_e72 a prov:Activity ; p-plan:correspondsToStep "src/harness/e72_edgegrain.py" ; prov:used :o_e52_aggregates ;
    rdfs:comment "Each ride's OWN recorded profile — no DEM error mixes in. One units bug caught in smoke: r1d_v2_edge returns kJ. The toll is e63's ride_tolls with the module floor set per call." .
:o_e72 a :Output ; dcterms:identifier "e72_edgegrain.csv" ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy :h_e72 ; :input :i_d36_fr_rider ; :transformer :F_v2edge, :F2, :F4, :F5 ;
    :cardinality 2039 ;
    :selection "per ride: v2Edge at pitches {5, 10, 30, 60, 90} m, its route-level twin (F2·ε_geom) at 5 m, the valley patch at 30 m, and the two F4 comparator rows" ;
    rdfs:comment "The F4-pub row reads (ε = 0.4094, c = 1.104) from e52_split.csv; the all-measured row reads c = 3.01 from e71_dem_pop.csv — both from producing CSVs, never literals. Also emits research/article/figs/fig-p3-scale.svg (hand-drawn)." .

:entry72 a :Statistic ; rdfs:label "Entry 72 — paper 3's first tranche: edge-grain fidelity, the scale U, the valley patch" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom :o_e72, :o_e52_split ; :gatedBy :gate ;
    rdfs:comment "Fidelity gap: the edge sum sits +1.83 pp above its own route-level integral at 5 m — bias-shaped, the stated bound A3's core claim needed (a3.divergence stays honestly PLANNED: needs real network routing). The scale U: 4.62/4.13/3.75/3.96/4.15 at 5→90 m — minimum exactly at the deployed 30 m; the bias zero near 60 m is aliasing cancelling noise, not accuracy. The valley patch takes 30 m from 3.75 · +1.33 to 3.29 · −0.08 (closer on 1,131/2,038, p < 1e-4). Paper 1's published F4 tops the whole table at 2.72 · −0.35 while the all-measured (ε_geom, article-2 c) pairing over-corrects to −3.80: the bundle rule extends to (ε, c) — individually-measured constants still travel in pairs. Gate section 3k." .

:h_e73 a prov:Activity ; p-plan:correspondsToStep "src/harness/e73_gridpath.py" ;
    prov:used :o_e52_aggregates, :o_e52_split, :OSM ;
    rdfs:comment "The E73 quantizer: each ride's GPS line followed onto the terrain raster's own lattice with the deployed move sets (classic-8 prefix, Farey levels {16:1, 32:2, 64:3, 128:4}, long moves sub-integrated). Two parity bugs its own gates forced out before the run of record: n = 1 positions must come from the raw geo track (double interpolation costs metres of phantom h+ on a noisy raster), and sample coordinates must go out at full js_str precision (%.8f cost 1.157 m of h+ on a 211 km ride). The same gates exposed that e41's published 30 m arms clip extrema (its 5 m regrid never aligns on real totals) — flagged for paper 2's errata ledger." .
:o_e73 a :Output ; dcterms:identifier "e73_gridpath.csv" ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy :h_e73 ; :input :i_d36_fr_rider ;
    :transformer :F_v2edge, :F1, :F2, :F3, :F4 ;
    :cardinality 1901 ;
    :selection "per ride x config (chain x directions n in {1,4,8,16,32,64,128} x portals): the deployed v2Edge, the flat-eps edge family eF1/eF2/eF4 (eF4 at the chain's measured c(tau=2) pin per region), the route forms F1-F4 (+F5f/patch, journal-only), quantizer QA (len_ratio, lateral p95, njump) and the per-chain noise pins cn_*. Populations all-arms-complete: IGC 1,034 - FABDEM 1,844" ;
    rdfs:comment "Every fitted constant read from its producing CSV (e52_split.csv, e63_split.E63_TAUN2p0.csv); c pins measured from geometry only and cross-checked against e71's CRATE rows (worst 0.14 m/km). Also emits research/article/figs/fig-p3-dirs.svg and fig-p3-chain.svg (hand-drawn)." .

:entry73 a :Statistic ; rdfs:label "Entry 73 — the discrete-routing ladder: directions, terrain lattice, portals, the eF family" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom :o_e73, :o_e52_split, :o_e71 ; :gatedBy :gate ;
    rdfs:comment "The dirs ladder is chain-shaped: on the smoothed IGC chain the n = 4/8 penalty is essentially all path-length inflation (len_ratio 1.2737/1.0543; P2 refuted there), on raw FABDEM it is almost all height noise (the lattice path reads 1.417x the polyline's h+ at n = 8). eF4 at the measured pin beats eF2 on all six DEM chains (P7 confirmed) and is the best deployable cost on FABDEM (41.62 vs 48.23). The deadband keeps a unique share at edge grain: F3 on the raw chain beats eF2 on the sigma-30-treated map on both populations (5.67 vs 9.21; 7.01 vs 11.49 — P8 refuted). Portals help 860/883 span-touched rides at sigma 10 (P4 confirmed). The flat-vs-geometric eps contest is chain-dependent: grade-local wins on smoothed chains, flat on raw FABDEM. Gate section 3l (27 gates)." .
